===Noun===
{{en-plural noun|head=[[alternate]] [[angles]]}}

# {{label|en|geometry}} the [[internal]] [[angle]]s made by two ([[parallel]]) lines with a third, on opposite sides of it. <br>If the parallels AB, CD, are cut by the line EF, [[intersect]]ing at points G and H, then the angles AGH, GHD, are called alternate angles (as also are the angles BGH and GHC).

